117 117 &amp; 1800 <pre><code>&lt;ModOp Property="ModuleOwner" Merge=".[FarmType='PlantFarm']"&gt;
  &lt;ModuleOwner&gt;
    &lt;ModuleBuildRadius&gt;20&lt;/ModuleBuildRadius&gt;
  &lt;/ModuleOwner&gt;
&lt;/ModOp&gt;
</code></pre> <pre><code>&lt;ModOp Type="merge" Path="//ModuleOwner/[FarmType='PlantFarm']"&gt;
  &lt;ModuleOwner&gt;
    &lt;ModuleBuildRadius&gt;20&lt;/ModuleBuildRadius&gt;
  &lt;/ModuleOwner&gt;
&lt;/ModOp&gt;
</code></pre> Only selects assets with the property in <code>assets.xml</code> <p>The lookup does not select assets without that property in <code>assets.xml</code>, even if it is part of their template or base asset."</p> <code>.</code> shortcut for <code>self::node()</code> <p>The use of <code>.[Condition]</code> is supported at the beginning of a <code>Path</code>, e.g. <code>Property="ModuleOwner" Merge=".[FarmType='PlantFarm']"</code>.</p> <p>The usage of <code>.</code> before brackets is not allowed in XPath 1.0 but in XPath 2.0. The modloader supports it by replacing it with <code>self::node()[Condition]</code>.</p>
